Source: https://magenta.tensorflow.org/datasets/groove

`grooveDrums.json` is a derived work. The original is 1,150 human drum
performances recorded on a Roland TD-11; this is those performances cut into
loopable excerpts of one, two and four bars, with the fills kept whole, and the
timing rounded from 480 ticks per quarter note to jamin's 24. Nothing was
generated, quantised onto a grid, or played by a machine. The metadata --
genre, tempo, time signature and whether a performance is a beat or a fill --
is the dataset's own.

The note numbers are the Roland TD-11's, unchanged. They are translated to
whatever kit is in use at playback time rather than in this file, so the
original mapping is preserved here. @see src/core/drumKits.js

CC BY 4.0 is one-way compatible with GPL-3.0, which is what the rest of jamin
is under. @see README.md "On bundling other people's collections"

Rebuild with:
  node scripts/extract_groove.mjs /path/to/groove
